{
  "style": "AUDIO PROFILE: The narrator of a 90-second demo video for a command-line data tool.\nTHE SCENE: A short story about a scientist whose data migration has to match exactly, watched by engineers and scientists.\nDIRECTOR'S NOTES:\n- Style: Confident and engaged, with real tension in the problem and relief at the end. Clear, never salesy.\n- Pace: Brisk and fast, like a good trailer. Crisp consonants. Short pauses inside a sentence.\n- Accent: Neutral American English.",
  "pause": 0.28,
  "tempo": 1.04,
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "text": "Maya is moving her weather station pipeline from IDL to Python.",
      "file": "hook-a8ca64f0f1f5.mp3",
      "seconds": 3.384,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "2f64e333c704b4b5017d1857077db6a6aa730ea23e1ec01f649a3ce66f4eb432"
    },
    {
      "id": "parity",
      "text": "The new output has to match the old. One to one.",
      "file": "parity-92ad585186c7.mp3",
      "seconds": 2.784,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "c5df72db2b4592a1a9b9c5508807033bf3a607b1949eee280d6a6cff282eff53"
    },
    {
      "id": "run",
      "text": "She runs both and compares. Every single row differs.",
      "file": "run-3b609c8ab0e7.mp3",
      "seconds": 3.336,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "c8bf80ef3a31abc2c0552dae65d66b0e2f739aeb98d5abb5166de84e002bdc26"
    },
    {
      "id": "floats",
      "text": "IDL works in 32-bit floats. Python works in 64.",
      "file": "floats-ca1bc5c59833.mp3",
      "seconds": 3.312,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "9ee779ddf766578251e3cf30d0d774bb233163d844b90350f889f313451a4187"
    },
    {
      "id": "noise",
      "text": "So the same humidity comes out two ways.",
      "file": "noise-3657759418a6.mp3",
      "seconds": 1.752,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "191ab05c01d800fa6dd2dad2d1d1d2560c1521f5aba8e153b42e7d8c2b792fb0"
    },
    {
      "id": "fill",
      "text": "IDL wrote minus 999 for a missing reading. Python writes nothing.",
      "file": "fill-f8f188c63fca.mp3",
      "seconds": 3.84,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "9fecdf9c0fca869f2cd9bfb5619482a24d9977b4155c03c99d6ab21703add35a"
    },
    {
      "id": "rename",
      "text": "She renamed temp to temperature_c, so a match by name quietly leaves it out.",
      "file": "rename-bf6c01bcea06.mp3",
      "seconds": 4.368,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "bef785802f269b579d85be62934af4e10e6f475155586e673acc2a0403c766a7"
    },
    {
      "id": "fix",
      "text": "And she fixed a real IDL bug. Station S3 had the wrong elevation, so its pressure changed on purpose.",
      "file": "fix-ae200e125ccf.mp3",
      "seconds": 5.424,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "751e1a3d6ecc30dfd163cb1243b2be44918c4a3717f9fe81334791dee8c2168d"
    },
    {
      "id": "doubt",
      "text": "Somewhere in all of that, the port has a bug of its own.",
      "file": "doubt-9649cdaf99f0.mp3",
      "seconds": 2.736,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "3b3dfee81c1b68a4b092a1da6753966b8b2fd6f8d1bda03b3917c2edeff57209"
    },
    {
      "id": "question",
      "text": "Which differences are fixes, and which are corruption?",
      "file": "question-1edbb55d5ed3.mp3",
      "seconds": 2.592,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "c6b64a826f751b6103dcafba6b8c69db496e450e19b9d8853105dbacabac4118"
    },
    {
      "id": "reveal",
      "text": "Veridelta compares two datasets on their keys, under rules you declare.",
      "file": "reveal-7e4e44fad997.mp3",
      "seconds": 3.672,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "a66ccc0e3675ab4b8bd2f8ac80a95ec722481c7071d6c8666951adcd571cae40"
    },
    {
      "id": "forgiven",
      "text": "Nothing is forgiven unless a rule says so.",
      "file": "forgiven-2b696f1fbf96.mp3",
      "seconds": 1.968,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "21ad32ad2527754c2f29b4020dfc7b4a056eff41f114f3c144e956d55e1d5dd2"
    },
    {
      "id": "declare",
      "text": "Maya declares the rename. Then veridelta suggest reads the data and proposes the rest.",
      "file": "declare-aac1416f2036.mp3",
      "seconds": 4.464,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "375a36ff85ee7cade335e0a5374746639084aa3b7e3c2761017b95eec493f06b"
    },
    {
      "id": "evidence",
      "text": "One rule for humidity: a tiny tolerance, and minus 999 as missing. It explains all 124 rows.",
      "file": "evidence-bee8006cdb1e.mp3",
      "seconds": 5.88,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "fe3b4055437e469f9717823347b783cae0839a261b3b9cb1824d5d8f32a105b4"
    },
    {
      "id": "model",
      "text": "No model is called.",
      "file": "model-70a63138804f.mp3",
      "seconds": 0.936,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "f2c3af1f2f9e1799d3939acecd9bb0857d3633674e4adeb249c076d1ddf86152"
    },
    {
      "id": "baseline",
      "text": "The pressure fix was on purpose, so a baseline accepts those 31 rows. Only those.",
      "file": "baseline-e1d9b9deacf6.mp3",
      "seconds": 4.248,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "b41ea2e024ce3ec028d0afbf1a76483bfb714a3bf06ad41560e14a2484173abe"
    },
    {
      "id": "left",
      "text": "What's left is the real bug. Four cold readings lost their minus sign.",
      "file": "left-076993f510fc.mp3",
      "seconds": 3.552,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "a673462602463a7e4d7c0ba9d2ccc5943ce224d3f3be70b78812f575866ff2e5"
    },
    {
      "id": "allalong",
      "text": "They were in the first rows all along.",
      "file": "allalong-fc576750f027.mp3",
      "seconds": 1.296,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "2468e43083efad1fd78b1f3efda912ebef4265c2dbfce72127bcf6de7edc5930"
    },
    {
      "id": "fails",
      "text": "The run fails, and in CI, so does the pull request.",
      "file": "fails-0cc307d261eb.mp3",
      "seconds": 2.616,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "be583eb64117cfcc64688377443259d72f97c98b2adb56d6b95905928147051c"
    },
    {
      "id": "passes",
      "text": "She fixes the port. It passes. One to one.",
      "file": "passes-f4aabf6536c5.mp3",
      "seconds": 2.664,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "e86206e0e62606552c7c44c6a5cb72d7a4d427cda4104d437a5170d5850bb8c1"
    },
    {
      "id": "end",
      "text": "Veridelta. Compare two datasets under rules you declare.",
      "file": "end-30c3666603f4.mp3",
